    {
      "id": 77974,
      "title": "Drug Take-Back Day",
      "url": "https://www.rockvillemd.gov/calendar/events/drug-take-back-day-2",
      "start_date": "2026-10-24 10:00:00",
      "end_date": "2026-10-24 14:00:00",
      "all_day": false,
      "description": "<p>The <a href=\"https://www.rockvillemd.gov/government/appointed-officials-and-departments/police-department/\">Rockville City Police Department</a> will offer a safe, free and anonymous way to dispose of unwanted prescription drugs, over-the-counter medicine and pet prescriptions on Saturday, Oct. 24, 2026.</p>\n<p>City police will accept unused and expired prescription drugs from 10 a.m.-2 p.m. in the <a href=\"https://www.rockvillemd.gov/places/rockville-city-police-station/\">Rockville City Police Station</a> parking lot at 2 W. Montgomery Ave. RCPD officers will be outside with easy drive-up and drop-off access, so there is no need to get out of your vehicle.</p>\n<p>Only pills and patches will be accepted. Liquids, needles, sharps, syringes, illicit drugs, glass containers and pressurized aerosols, such as inhalers, cannot be accepted. Bring medication in original containers or combine pills in a clear, sealed plastic bag for disposal. Collected medication will be safely destroyed.</p>",
